Linux boot image for the SiTAR serial smoke test
================================================

The image is downloaded separately, not committed as generated simulator output.
Source repository: https://github.com/adhuliya/ajit-toolchain
Branch: ajit-linux
Path: os/Ajit_linux/linux_boot/testing_in_proress/22_0ct_21/c-model/boot_loader_plus_kernel.mmap

From this directory, download and verify:

    curl --fail --location --output boot_loader_plus_kernel.mmap https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adhuliya/ajit-toolchain/ajit-linux/os/Ajit_linux/linux_boot/testing_in_proress/22_0ct_21/c-model/boot_loader_plus_kernel.mmap
    echo '2bcc0ec62dbf3dac5d63c631effd10040442ffd3980e0b46e0de82ea978b78cf  boot_loader_plus_kernel.mmap' | sha256sum --check
    bash ../serial_boot_smoke/build.sh

Do not use the image if hash verification fails. The build script also verifies
this hash before staging main.mmap. The matching kernel disassembly is in
kernel/kernel_objdump.txt. Use init PC 0xf0000000. See the modular simulator
README for sync/async boot commands and their different cycle budgets.
